= Content moderation =

== Overview ==
'''Content moderation''' is the set of processes by which a platform or community applies rules to user-generated content, accounts, or interactions.

Moderation can include review, labeling, ranking changes, visibility limits, removal, account restrictions, appeals, and enforcement automation. Decisions may be made by users, moderators, automated systems, or combinations of them.

A moderation action expresses application of a rule or policy. By itself it does not prove that the moderated content is false, harmful, illegal, or otherwise invalid outside that policy context.

== Boundaries ==
* content moderation ≠ fact-checking necessarily
* moderation action ≠ proof of falsity
* content moderation ≠ one enforcement action only

